# Agent Management System

How it works
init_agents: Initializes the agent list with predefined data.

print_active_agents: Iterates through the list and prints information for agents where status == 1.


A simple C-based program to manage and filter a list of agents using structures.

## Features
- **Data Structuring**: Uses a `struct` to organize agent data (codename, status, and name).
- **Modularity**: Logic is separated into initialization and display functions.
- **Filtering**: Automatically filters and displays only agents with an active status.

## How to Compile
You can compile this program using `gcc`:

```bash
gcc main.c -o agent_system
./agent_system

#include <stdio.h> 
#include <string.h>

struct Agent {
    int codename;
    int status;
    char name[20];
};
    
void print_active_agents(struct Agent agency[],int size){
    
     for(int i = 0; i < size;i++){
        if(agency[i].status == 1){
            printf("All agents with status == 1: %d\n",agency[i].codename);
            printf("Name of agents that have status == 1: %s\n",agency[i].name);
        }
    } 

}

void init_agents(struct Agent agency[]) {
    agency[0].codename = 707;
    agency[1].codename = 550;
    agency[2].codename  = 889; 

    agency[0].status = 1;
    agency[1].status = 1;
    agency[2].status = 0; 

    strcpy(agency[0].name,"Smith");
    strcpy(agency[1].name,"Bob");
    strcpy(agency[2].name,"Will");
}

int main() {
    struct Agent agency[3];
    init_agents(agency);
    print_active_agents(agency,3);


    return 0;
}
